# Line-ending and whitespace policy
#
# Text files use LF. Cargo fmt, rustfmt, and this repo's git whitespace check
# (`git diff --check`) assume LF; the small set of legacy CRLF files is being
# normalized as they are touched (see crates/*/Cargo.toml 2026-08-04).
#
# Windows batch files keep CRLF: cmd.exe continuation/`goto` parsing is
# safest with CRLF line endings.
#
# Raw binary fixtures are byte-exact and must never be normalized or
# re-encoded; their provenance is pinned by `mida.fixture-provenance/v1`.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.bin binary
